This crate contains no code derived from LiveKit. It depends on sew-lk-compat (Apache-2.0),
which holds code ported from livekit/client-sdk-js (Copyright 2021 LiveKit, Inc.), and on
sew-lkproto (Apache-2.0), which holds code generated from livekit/protocol (Copyright 2023
LiveKit, Inc.); both carry LiveKit's NOTICE text. Through sew-e2ee it also depends on
sew-mls-crypto (MIT OR Apache-2.0), which holds code derived from openmls_rust_crypto (part of
OpenMLS, MIT) and carries OpenMLS's MIT licence text. A binary that includes sew-call-client
includes all three and must carry their NOTICE files.

The `rust-crypto` feature's DTLS/SRTP provider (src/rust_crypto.rs) follows the str0m-rust-crypto
crate of str0m (https://github.com/algesten/str0m, Copyright Martin Algesten, MIT OR
Apache-2.0).

Its WebRTC stack is sew-str0m and sew-str0m-is, Alakazam Labs' fork of str0m
(https://github.com/Alakazam-211/str0m, MIT OR Apache-2.0, str0m's copyright and licence texts
kept), with str0m's own str0m-proto and str0m-aws-lc-rs from crates.io (MIT OR Apache-2.0).
Those two crates.io packages carry no licence file; their text is str0m's LICENSE-MIT.txt at
tag 0.25.0 (https://github.com/algesten/str0m/blob/0.25.0/LICENSE-MIT.txt).

